setup: work/index.mjs = OLD (gh-CLI) generation
swap: work/index.mjs overwritten with NEW (REST) generation while child A is in flight
child-A (spawned before the swap, importing throughout): [
  { event: 'first-import', generation: 'old-gh-cli' },
  {
    event: 'second-import-same-process',
    generation: 'old-gh-cli',
    sameModuleObject: true
  }
]
child-B (spawned after the swap): [
  { event: 'first-import', generation: 'new-rest-api' },
  {
    event: 'second-import-same-process',
    generation: 'new-rest-api',
    sameModuleObject: true
  }
]

result: child A stayed on "old-gh-cli" -> "old-gh-cli" across the swap (module-cache identity preserved: true); child B (post-swap) loaded "new-rest-api".
PASS: an in-flight process is unaffected by a concurrent on-disk runtime swap; only a fresh process picks up the new generation.
